1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,500
This is Learning Line, a concept prototype for TMMIN Karawang.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:12,000
We follow one sealer defect from the camera to a revised standard, and show who decides at every step.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:17,000
A repurposed camera checks every sealer bead.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,500
The model learned only from good beads, so it flags anything that departs from them and marks where.

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:30,000
The alert goes to the station that made the defect, not to final inspection.

6
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:34,500
The operator confirms. A false alarm would be rejected with a reason,

7
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:40,000
and only a rejection the team leader verifies can update the model.

8
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:47,500
The confirmation raises a yellow andon for the team leader, with a suggestion:

9
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,500
stop and fix, because the defect is leak-critical.

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:59,000
The system never stops the line. The team leader does, logs a note, and restarts it after the repair.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Station 2 is over its false-alarm budget, so its model goes to review, but confirmed defects are never hidden.

12
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:14,500
Every station camera is on one wall.

13
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:20,000
The shift timeline replays each alert next to the decision people made, and faces are masked at the edge.

14
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:30,000
When the same defect is confirmed a third time in a shift, a Kaizen ticket opens on its own, with the three alerts attached.

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:38,000
AI only drafts the background and the current condition, and says so.

16
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:43,000
Here is a ticket that has finished its countermeasure trial.

17
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The engineer requests validation, and the senior expert validates the knowledge card.

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,000
It now revises the standard, and yokoten carries it to every station running the same process.

19
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:07,000
From any screen, the assistant answers only from validated knowledge cards, and cites the card it used.

20
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:18,000
When no card covers a question, it says so, and routes it to the owner engineer instead of guessing.

21
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:25,000
Management watches the Gate 1 indicators as distance to target.

22
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Every number says where it comes from: the thirty-one percent baseline is case data, the move toward twenty-four is simulated history, and Gate 1 is not reached yet.

23
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:43,500
AI detects and drafts. People decide.

24
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:50,000
Learning Line, a concept prototype on simulated data.
